+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`TaskList.add` already validates title, priority and tags (`invalid-input`) and rejects duplicate titles (`duplicate`), leaving the list untouched on failure. The domain must not throw, read the clock or use randomness.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Parse lines and reuse `list.add`, so import rules never drift from the add rules.
+- Report every rejected line with its number and a human-readable reason.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Quoting or escaping `;` inside titles, CSV dialects, or exporting.
+- All-or-nothing import: valid lines are kept even when others are rejected.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Pure module `src/domain/import.ts` exporting `importTasks(list: TaskList, text: string): ImportReport`; re-exported from `src/index.ts` with the `ImportReport` and `RejectedLine` types. It never throws.
+- Split `text` on `\r\n`, `\n` or `\r`. Line numbers count every line, blank ones included, so they match what the user sees in the spreadsheet or editor. A line that is empty or only whitespace is skipped and is neither imported nor rejected.
+- Split each line on `;` into at most three fields: title, priority, tags. Fewer fields are fine (`Buy milk` or `Buy milk;high`). More than three fields is rejected as `invalid-input` ("too many fields"), so a stray `;` is not silently swallowed.
+- Priority is trimmed; empty means `normal`. It is otherwise validated by `add` (case-sensitive, as everywhere else).
+- Tags: the tags field is trimmed and split on runs of whitespace; an empty field means no tags. Duplicates are collapsed by `add`.
+- Each task goes through `list.add`; its error message becomes `reason`. A title already in the list, or on an earlier line, is rejected by `add` as a duplicate, and the earlier one stays.
+- `rejected.line` is the 1-based number; `reason` is a string; entries are in line order.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Titles containing `;` cannot be imported (they are rejected for having too many fields or mis-parsed as priority, which is rejected as invalid).
