+## Why
+
+Teams moving to Tidy Tasks from spreadsheets have many tasks to enter. Adding them one by one is slow, so the package needs a bulk import from pasted text.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add a public helper `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- `text` holds one task per line as `title;priority;tags` (priority may be empty for `normal`; tags separated by spaces). Blank lines are skipped.
+- It adds every valid line to the list and returns `{ imported, rejected }`, where `rejected` lists `{ line, reason }` for each line not added, `line` counting from 1.
+- Nothing changes in the existing list API.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-import`: bulk import of tasks from text lines into a task list, with a per-line report of what was rejected.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/domain/import.ts`; new export in `src/index.ts`; tests in `test/`; a README paragraph.
+- No new dependency.
